      "problem": "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\nz=\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{25}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $O$ is given by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}},\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is a hyperbolic paraboloid with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,-1,0),\\,a=5,\\,b=4.\n$$",
