      "problem": "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1,\\,-\\infty <x<\\infty .\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of an elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThus, an elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is an elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis and $b=c=1.$",
